  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Seafood investor Thomas Jessen helped develop Kverva’s portfolio after a salmon-sausage venture failed to win over shoppers. The company exchanged its production line for shares in Lofotprodukt, then supplied capital for acquisitions. That business became a foundation for Insula, bringing together producers across the Nordic region.\n\nJessen’s team worked with businesses on acquisitions, strategy and entry into new markets. Kverva used knowledge gained through SalMar alongside analysis of seafood demand, taking an active role after investing. Jessen accepted that some ventures would fail; he considered the willingness to back uncertain ideas necessary to finding successful ones.",
    "html": "<p>Seafood investor Thomas Jessen helped develop Kverva’s portfolio after a salmon-sausage venture failed to win over shoppers. The company exchanged its production line for shares in Lofotprodukt, then supplied capital for acquisitions. That business became a foundation for Insula, bringing together producers across the Nordic region.</p>\r\n<p>Jessen’s team worked with businesses on acquisitions, strategy and entry into new markets. Kverva used knowledge gained through SalMar alongside analysis of seafood demand, taking an active role after investing. Jessen accepted that some ventures would fail; he considered the willingness to back uncertain ideas necessary to finding successful ones.</p>\r\n",
